From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:09:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] init: extra_free_kbytes.sh: multiply before dividing the
 margin

When a zone's own margin wins, the script computes the new
watermark_scale_factor as

    base_margin / (managed / 10000) + watermark_delta

in bc at scale 0, so managed / 10000 is truncated first: the term is
inflated by up to a factor of two for a zone of under 20000 pages, and
bc divides by zero for a zone of under 10000 pages, leaving an empty
value that the following test cannot compare. watermark_scale_factor
is a fraction of managed in units of 1/10000, so compute
base_margin * 10000 / managed instead.

Tried on a PC with the script reading saved files: the Raspberry Pi 5
AAOS guest's /proc/zoneinfo (3 GiB, 2026-10-17) gives 119 against 120
before; a zoneinfo with zones of 15000 and 9000 managed pages gave
"Divide by zero" and a test error before, and a value without errors
now.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 init/extra_free_kbytes.sh | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/init/extra_free_kbytes.sh b/init/extra_free_kbytes.sh
index 0edaab2..1dcd379 100755
--- a/init/extra_free_kbytes.sh
+++ b/init/extra_free_kbytes.sh
@@ -136,7 +136,10 @@ do
     then
         watermark_scale_new=$(echo "$watermark_scale + $watermark_delta" | bc)
     else
-        watermark_scale_new=$(echo "$base_margin / (${managed[i]} / 10000) + $watermark_delta" | bc)
+        # Multiply before dividing: bc runs this at scale 0, and managed / 10000
+        # truncated first inflates the result (up to twice for a zone of under 20000
+        # pages) and divides by zero for one of under 10000.
+        watermark_scale_new=$(echo "$base_margin * 10000 / ${managed[i]} + $watermark_delta" | bc)
     fi
 
     if [ $max_watermark_scale -lt $watermark_scale_new ]
